-- title:
--   Twisted tower from a formal group and a 2-cocycle
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime such that $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal{O}$, the ideal $(p)$ is maximal and $\mathcal{O}$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $\Phi$ be a commutative $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal{O}$ (a $d$-tuple of power series in $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ variables with vanishing constant term, identity linear terms, associative, and invariant under swapping the two blocks of variables), and suppose that over $\mathcal{O}/(p)$ the quotient of $(\mathcal{O}/(p))[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ by the ideal generated by the components of the $p$-th iterate `nthSeries p` of the reduction of $\Phi$ has $\mathcal{O}/(p)$-dimension $p^{h}$. Let $E$ be a tower of commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, each finite and free, with bialgebra transitions $st_v : E_{v+1}\to E_v$ that are surjective, with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}} E_v = p^{v\cdot he}$ and $\ker st_v$ equal to `torsionIdeal` at $p^{v}$, i.e. the image of the augmentation ideal of $E_{v+1}$ under the $p^{v}$-th convolution power of the identity. Let $c_2(v)\in (E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}} E_v)^{d}$ satisfy the following block of hypotheses: compatibility $(st_v\otimes st_v)(c_2(v+1)_i)=c_2(v)_i$; divisibility $c_2(v)_i\in (p)$; and, for every $\mathcal{O}$-algebra $g$ in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor and which is $(p)$-adically complete, normalisation (specialising one tensor factor along an algebra map $f:E_v\to g$ and the other along the counit gives $0$, in both orders), symmetry in the two points, and the $\Phi$-cocycle identity relating the three-point expressions, all evaluated by $(p)$-adic evaluation of $\Phi$. Then there exists a tower $L$ of commutative cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal{O}$-algebras, each finite and free, together with bialgebra transitions $t_v:L_{v+1}\to L_v$, bialgebra maps $\iota_v : E_v\to L_v$ and $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps $\Psi_v : \mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to L_v$ such that each $t_v$ is surjective, $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathcal{O}} L_v = p^{v(h+he)}$, $\ker t_v$ is the $p^{v}$-torsion ideal of $L_{v+1}$, $t_v\circ\iota_{v+1}=\iota_v\circ st_v$, $t_v\circ\Psi_{v+1}=\Psi_v$, each $\Psi_v(X_i)$ lies in the radical of $(p)$ in $L_v$ with $\Psi_v$ given on every $F$ by $(p)$-adic evaluation at the $\Psi_v(X_i)$, the counit kills $\Psi_v(X_i)$, $\Psi_v$ of the $i$-th component of `nthSeries` $(p^{v})$ of $\Phi$ lies in $(p)$, the induced map $E_v\otimes_{\mathcal{O}}\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]\to L_v$ is surjective, and the comultiplication is twisted by the cocycle: $\Delta(\Psi_v(X_i))$ equals the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $\Phi_i$ at $\bigl(\Psi_v(X_j)\otimes 1\bigr)_j$ and at the $(p)$-adic evaluation of $\Phi_j$ at $\bigl(1\otimes\Psi_v(X_k)\bigr)_k$ and $\bigl((\iota_v\otimes\iota_v)(c_2(v)_k)\bigr)_k$.
--
--   This is the level-by-level construction, in Fontaine's style, of a $p$-divisible tower realising an extension of the étale tower $(E_v)$ by the formal group $\Phi$, the extension class being carried by the symmetric normalised $2$-cocycle $c_2$; the affine algebras $L_v$ are presented as $E_v\,\hat\otimes\,\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ with comultiplication twisted by $c_2$. It is used in the construction of the $p$-divisible group attached to a Honda system with split coordinates.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_pDivisibleTower_of_cocycle.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PDivisibleGroup_Basic
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_BasicV2
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_EndRingV2
import Definitions.Def_MvFormalGroup_NegV2
